<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  Panasonic FS-A1GT 4MB — DOS2 variant.

  Identical to "Panasonic FS-A1GT 4MB.xml" except slot 3-2: instead of the Sony HB-F1XD disk ROM
  (MSX-DOS 1 only), this pack carries the machine's own 64 KB turbo R disk ROM with
  its TC8566AF driver replaced by the WD2793 driver from that same Sony ROM, so the
  built-in MSX-DOS 2.31 kernel runs on the controller this core implements.  The ROM
  is 4 x 16 KB banks selected by a write to 7FF0h, which needs the TURBOR_FDC block
  type (mapper MAPPER_TRFDC) and a core built with it — older cores will not run it.

  Built 2026-09-23.  Verified in openMSX against the reference FS-A1ST/FS-A1GT:
  Illusion City and SD Snatcher follow the same path as on the real machines
  (boot sector called, bank 3 handover, no stack damage).  Synthesis and patch list:
  docs/turbor_diskrom_20260923.md, tools/turbor_diskrom/.
-->
<!--
  Panasonic FS-A1GT (1992, Japanese MSX turbo R) — the last officially released MSX.
  Stock RAM is 512 KB; this variant only changes the 3-0 mapper size to 4MB
  (block_count is in 16 KB units: 32=512KB, 64=1MB, 128=2MB, 256=4MB).

  Slot layout follows openMSX share/machines/Panasonic_FS-A1GT.xml.  On the real
  machine every internal ROM lives in ONE 4 MB image (fs-a1gt_firmware.rom,
  sha1 e779c338...), addressed in 8 KB blocks; the skip values below are that
  file's byte offsets, taken from openMSX's firstblock numbers:

      blocks 40-43  = 0x50000  MAIN BIOS + BASIC   (32 KB, starts F3 C3 = DI/JP)
      blocks 48-55  = 0x60000  disk ROM + MSX-DOS2 (64 KB, TC8566AF driver)
      blocks 56-57  = 0x70000  SUB ROM             (16 KB, "CD")
      blocks 58-61  = 0x74000  Kanji driver+BASIC  (32 KB, "AB")
      blocks 62-63  = 0x7C000  MSX-MUSIC           (16 KB, "AB")

  Four things the real machine has that this core cannot represent:

  1. The R800 CPU.  This pack ships the genuine turbo R MAIN BIOS, so MSXVER
     (0002Dh) reads 3 and software concludes "turbo R".  turbo R-only titles will
     therefore start and then execute R800-only opcodes (MULUB/MULUW), which a
     plain Z80 swallows as NOPs.  Use this pack only on a build with R800 support;
     on a stock build prefer an MSX2+ pack for MSX2+ software.

  2. The 4 MB built-in software in slot 3-3 (MSX View, etc.).  It needs the
     PANASONIC mapper plus 32 KB SRAM, neither of which exists in createMSXpack's
     BLOCK_TYPES nor package.sv's mapper_typ_t.  Omitted; 3-3 is left empty.

  3. The floppy controller.  The real FS-A1GT has a TC8566AF (uPD765 family) with
     its driver inside the 0x60000 block above.  This core implements only a
     WD2793 (rtl/peripheral/wd1793.sv), so that driver would hang before DOS.
     Slot 3-2 carries a WD2793 disk ROM instead (sha1 12f2cc79..., the same bytes
     the working Sony HB-F1XV pack loads) — proven on hardware in the FS-A1F pack.
     The tradeoff: this is no longer an authentic FS-A1GT disk subsystem, and the
     machine's own DOS 2 2.31 is gone; the pack runs MSX-DOS 1 from that disk ROM.
     (An ASCII MSX-DOS 2.20 kernel used to sit in 3-3.  Removed 2026-09-23: with
     DOS 2.20 active, SD Snatcher never gets its boot sector called and Illusion
     City loads through a path that overwrites its own stack.  Measured in
     openMSX against the reference machines, and confirmed on the board.)

  4. MIDI (the GT's built-in interface) and the PCM sampler.  No RTL exists for
     either; software that requires them will not find them.

  The Opening ROM (blocks 36-37) IS carried, in slot 0-3 at 4000h.  Do not judge it
  by its first bytes: it starts with FFh and has no AB header, but the turbo R BIOS
  calls into it by a hard-coded address during boot (blank from 4000h to 78FFh but holds 1673 bytes of code from 7900h).
  Leaving it out makes that call read FFh = RST 38 and the machine never reaches
  VDP init; measured against openMSX, which calls 7900h in slot 0-3 at t=0.599 s.
-->
<msxConfig>
  <type>MSX2</type>
  <kbd_layout></kbd_layout>
  <device typ="KANJI" id="Kanji ROM">
    <rom>
      <filename>fs-a1gt_kanjifont.rom</filename>
      <!-- lowercase <sha1> here: createMSXpack reads block/SHA1 but device/rom/sha1
           (createMSXpack.py:186 vs :238).  Getting it wrong is fail-quiet. -->
      <sha1>5aff2d9b6efc723bc395b0f96f0adfa83cc54a49</sha1>
    </rom>
  </device>
  <device typ="RESET_STATUS" id="Reset Status register"></device>
  <!-- The GT does carry the Matsushita switched device on I/O 0x40/0x41 (firmware
       switch, kanji).  On turbo R it is NOT the 5.37 MHz turbo — that machine
       switches CPUs instead — but the port itself is present, so it is declared. -->
  <device typ="MATSUSHITA" id="Matsushita switched I/O"></device>
  <device typ="MOONSOUND" id="MoonSound PCM Wave ROM"></device>
  <!-- The GT has a built-in MSX-MIDI interface.  Its BIOS services it from inside
       the interrupt handler (1A74 in a,(0E9h) / and 02h / call nz,0FF75h), so a core
       that leaves E9h floating at FFh calls the MIDI hooks on every interrupt.  The
       ST has no MIDI and its BIOS has no such poll, which is why only the GT needs
       this.  openMSX returns 05h (TxRDY|TxEMPTY, RxRDY clear) here. -->
  <device typ="MIDI" id="MSX-MIDI"></device>
  <primary slot="0">
    <secondary slot="0">
      <block start="0" id="MSX BIOS with BASIC ROM">
        <type>ROM</type>
        <block_count>2</block_count>
        <filename>fs-a1gt_firmware.rom</filename>
        <SHA1>e779c338eb91a7dea3ff75f3fde76b8af22c4a3a</SHA1>
        <skip>327680</skip>
      </block>
    </secondary>
    <secondary slot="2">
      <block start="1" id="MSX Music">
        <type>MSX-MUSIC</type>
        <block_count>1</block_count>
        <filename>fs-a1gt_firmware.rom</filename>
        <SHA1>e779c338eb91a7dea3ff75f3fde76b8af22c4a3a</SHA1>
        <skip>507904</skip>
      </block>
    </secondary>
    <secondary slot="3">
      <block start="1" id="MSX Opening ROM">
        <type>ROM</type>
        <block_count>1</block_count>
        <filename>fs-a1gt_firmware.rom</filename>
        <SHA1>e779c338eb91a7dea3ff75f3fde76b8af22c4a3a</SHA1>
        <skip>294912</skip>
      </block>
    </secondary>
  </primary>
  <primary slot="1">
    <secondary slot="0">
      <block start="0">
        <type>SLOT A</type>
      </block>
    </secondary>
  </primary>
  <primary slot="2">
    <secondary slot="0">
      <block start="0">
        <type>SLOT B</type>
      </block>
    </secondary>
  </primary>
  <primary slot="3">
    <secondary slot="0">
      <block start="0" id="Main RAM">
        <type>RAM MAPPER</type>
        <block_count>256</block_count>
        <pattern>4</pattern>
      </block>
    </secondary>
    <secondary slot="1">
      <block start="0" id="MSX Sub ROM">
        <type>ROM</type>
        <block_count>1</block_count>
        <filename>fs-a1gt_firmware.rom</filename>
        <SHA1>e779c338eb91a7dea3ff75f3fde76b8af22c4a3a</SHA1>
        <skip>458752</skip>
      </block>
      <block start="1" id="MSX Kanji Driver with BASIC">
        <type>ROM</type>
        <block_count>2</block_count>
        <filename>fs-a1gt_firmware.rom</filename>
        <SHA1>e779c338eb91a7dea3ff75f3fde76b8af22c4a3a</SHA1>
        <skip>475136</skip>
      </block>
    </secondary>
    <secondary slot="2">
      <block start="1" id="turbo R disk ROM (DOS 2.31 kernel, WD2793 driver)">
        <type>TURBOR_FDC</type>
        <block_count>4</block_count>
        <filename>fs-a1gt_diskrom_wd2793.rom</filename>
        <SHA1>86f81c71c858d98e2d4031566efd3b5a3843e279</SHA1>
      </block>
    </secondary>
  </primary>
</msxConfig>
